        "source": "import triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n@triton.jit\ndef bias_add_relu(X, B, Y, TOTAL: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(0)\n    offs = pid * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    mask = offs < TOTAL\n    x = tl.load(X + offs, mask, other=0.0)\n    b = tl.load(B + (offs % N), mask, other=0.0)\n    r = x + b\n    r = tl.maximum(r, 0.0)\n    tl.store(Y + offs, r, mask)\n",
        "rationale": "Fused bias_add and relu into a single kernel launch to reduce kernel launch overhead and improve memory locality. Increased num_warps to 8 and num_stages to 2 to better hide latency and improve instruction pipelining on NVIDIA A100. This reduces memory traffic by performing both operations in a single pass, improving throughput and lowering latency."
      },
